course: dictionary
lesson: 8034
title: Refund: money back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A refund is money given back to you. Read the words around it: «You kept the receipt, so the shop gave you a refund.» Receipt and given back tell you the shop paid your money back. Refund can be a noun (a refund) or a verb (to refund someone).
explain: Maths uses refunds too. If you spend ten dollars and get a refund of four, you are only six dollars down, because ten take away four is six. To check a meaning, swap in "money given back" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Ask for a full refund» tells you that you want all of your money back. Shops have rules about refunds, and they usually ask for the receipt first. Those clues help you know what the word means in that place.
explain: Scammers use the word refund to trick people. A message that says «You have won a refund, send your PIN now!» is urgent and asks for a secret number. Real shops do not need your PIN to give you money back, so stop and ask a grown-up.
fact: A refund is money given back to you, usually because you returned something you bought or a service did not happen.
fact: To refund someone is to give them their money back.
fact: Shops usually ask for the receipt before they give a refund.
fact: «A faulty item can be taken back to be exchanged or refunded.»
fact: Scams may ask for your PIN or password, or promise a refund you never expected. Real businesses never ask to be paid with gift cards.
exercise: «You kept the receipt, so the shop gave you a refund.» What is a refund? | *Money given back to you | A gift card for your birthday | A list of the things you bought | A new item you get for free
exercise: In maths, you spent ten dollars and got a refund of four. How much are you down now? | Ten dollars | *Six dollars | Fourteen dollars | Four dollars
exercise: «Ask for a full refund.» What does full refund mean? | *All of your money back | A free holiday | Half of your money back | Money to spend in another shop only
test: Gran says, «I will refund you for the broken toy.» What does refund mean here? | To throw the broken toy away | To buy a new toy for someone | *To give you your money back | To wrap a present
test: Which message is a scam? | «Please keep the receipt for the faulty kettle.» | «Your receipt is in the bag, thank you for shopping.» | *«You have won a refund! Send your PIN to claim it now.» | «The shop is open until six o'clock.»
exam: Why should you keep the receipt? | *Shops usually ask for it before they give a refund | Receipts are good for marking your place in a book | Receipts stop the shop from closing | A receipt is a type of gift card
